      "structure": "A steel lattice dome, 32 m (105 ft) high and 300 m (984 ft) across, on a concrete ring; concrete arms around it.",
      "look": "A cross-shaped terminal with a great shallow dome of triangulated glass and titanium at its centre, glowing amber at night like a beacon for travellers from other decks; the four arms are low and dark.",
      "entrances": "Kerb entrance from the Terminal Road; link from the arrival gates on the port side; deck lifts below the dome.",
      "capacity": "About 12,000 transfer travellers an hour.",
      "services": "Deck lifts under the dome, baggage transfer belts, 6 stair and lift cores.",
      "interior": "A domed great hall at the crossing of four arms: deck transfer desks, ticketing and lounges in the bow arm, shuttle booking and baggage transfer in the stern arm, the link to the gates on the port side and the kerb hall on the landside. Food court and business lounges upstairs; deck lifts and baggage belts below."
